Subject: winecoreaudio: per-stream volume, DefaultOutput routing, callback-driven events, GetDevicePosition, SetSampleRate, and channel layouts

1. Replace hardware kAudioDevicePropertyVolumeScalar calls in unix_set_volumes()
   with per-stream software PCM scaling (volume_scale.h, applied in ca_render_cb)
   across FLOAT32, PCM16, PCM24, PCM32, and PCM8 with unity/mute fast paths.
   WASAPI stream volume/mute no longer clobbers macOS host system volume and now
   works on HDMI/USB/Bluetooth outputs that lack hardware volume controls.
2. Open kAudioUnitSubType_DefaultOutput (without pinning CurrentDevice) when a
   render stream targets the current macOS default output device, so connecting
   or disconnecting AirPods/headphones or switching system output re-routes live
   game audio seamlessly without restarting. Resolve the live default device in
   unix_get_latency().
3. For pinned non-default / capture streams, register a CoreAudio
   kAudioDevicePropertyDeviceIsAlive listener (lock-only + Mach semaphore wake,
   no Wine syscalls from foreign threads) and return AUDCLNT_E_DEVICE_INVALIDATED
   once unplugged.
4. Drive AUDCLNT_STREAMFLAGS_EVENTCALLBACK from CoreAudio RT render/capture
   callbacks via a Mach semaphore bridged to unix_timer_loop() (Wine thread)
   while playing, and fall back to periodic semaphore timeout pacing after
   Stop()/Reset() until Release() to match Windows WASAPI behavior (passing all
   4,459 mmdevapi:render tests with 0 failures).
5. Defer AudioOutputUnitStart() from unix_create_stream() to unix_start() and
   stop the AudioUnit in unix_stop() (outside stream->lock to avoid lock-order
   inversion with RT callbacks), eliminating idle RT audio thread overhead.
6. Implement IAudioClock2::GetDevicePosition (params->device == TRUE in
   unix_get_position()) returning raw hardware frames instead of E_NOTIMPL.
7. Implement IAudioClockAdjustment::SetSampleRate (unix_set_sample_rate(),
   wired in both 64-bit and WoW64 unix call tables) with live AudioUnit
   reconfiguration, error recovery, and synchronized unix_get_frequency().
8. Parse CoreAudio kAudioChannelLayoutTag_* (bitmap, Mono, Stereo/Headphones/
   Binaural, Quad, 5.1, 7.1, and generic channel-count tags) in
   unix_get_mix_format().

